{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964","id":3585595027,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7Vt9aT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118964.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118964","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118964/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118964/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/816ef8041dfead9028e590777b206f0c996177ee","number":118964,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Allow selecting the interface for Multicast in `PacketPeerUDP`","user":{"login":"NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev","html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Summary of changes\r\nAdded the function `set_multicast_send_interface(if_name)` to `PacketPeerUDP` and `NetSocket`.\r\nThis allows controlling the interface, through which a packet is sent to a multicast address.\r\nBefore, the OS would choose an interface, so that the packet can reach it, but since it is a multicast address, it would choose a random one (so for example localhost or dummy0), which is useless, because the address can be reached using any interface.\r\nInternally, this sets `IPV6_MULTICAST_IF` and/or `IP_MULTICAST_IF` using `setsockopt(...)`.\r\n\r\n### Example usage\r\nThis allows sending packets to multicast addresses using all interfaces:\r\n<img width=\"771\" height=\"661\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5fe6194d-b878-4c0d-a573-cca0f440a1d4\" />\r\n\r\n### Motivation\r\nThis is an implementation of https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/3109\r\nAlso, I myself have had the same problem with multicast, so I decided to fix it.\r\nWithout this, functions like `join_mutlicast_group` in Godot are a bit (or a lot) useless, because the interface choices by the OS aren't consistent.\r\n\r\n### Technical overview\r\nThe user calls set_mutlicast_send_interface(interface_name) on the PacketPeerUDP, which will pass the argument to the underlaying NetSocket. Each platform group (Unix, Windows), then defines that function in its own way, but the main priciple is the same:\r\nIf the socket ip_type covers IPv6, we find the interface index and call `setsockopt(_sock, IPPROTO_IPV6, IPV6_MULTICAST_IF, ...)` with it.\r\nIf the socket ip_type covers IPv4, we find the first IPv4 address in the interface and call `setsockopt(_sock, IPPROTO_IP, IP_MULTICAST_IF, ...)` with it.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\nI have tested it, these connections worked first try (aside from firewall config):\r\n1) Localhost (Almost any interface works locally)\r\n2) Windows - WSL (Linux), using vEthernet (Hyper-V connection)\r\n3) Windows - Windows, using Wi-Fi\r\n4) Windows - Android, using Wi-Fi\r\n5) Android - Android, using Wi-Fi\r\n6) Windows - Ubuntu VM (VMWare Drivers)\r\n\r\n### Discussion\r\nI am not sure if it works on iOS and MacOS, so testing with it could be good.\r\n\r\n### AI Self Disclosure\r\nThe `setsockopt(...)` lines were written by Claude. I made sure that the code makes sense, is readable and actually works, which means that I made changes to it.\r\n\r\nEDIT: I have read the documentation for setsockopt parameters, and made changes according to it. It's a bit cleaner and safer now, and I can say that all code in this is written by a human (everything that AI originally wrote isn't in the code).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starre